# TASK-MVP-004B - found empirically, not hypothetical: the Docker build
# context is the /opt/estore/app/ deployment directory itself, which is
# also where the server-only secrets/ directory and the real (non-.example)
# mysql-init SQL file live, sitting alongside the tracked source. Without
# these exclusions, `COPY . .` bakes real database passwords directly into
# the estore-app image's filesystem layers - confirmed live via
# `docker run --rm estore-app find / -iname '*mysql_root_password*'`
# finding the file inside a freshly built image before this fix.
secrets/
docker/production/mysql-init/*.sql
